{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448215-the-ship-of-terror-world-of-darkness-prelude-act","id":1448215,"title":"The ship of terror (world of darkness, prelude act)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-11T07:49:37-07:00","id":1448215,"title":"The ship of terror (world of darkness, prelude act)","content":"Hi there! I'm writing an adventure set in 1850, in London, in a &quot;world of darkness&quot; style: storical event mixed with sovrannatural things. And i ask for your help! The PCs would leave London with the &quot;Rescue expedition&quot; who set sail in order to find &quot;The Franklin expedition&quot;, aka &quot;the terror&quot; and &quot;the erebus&quot; who left London in 1845. Why they have to? Because for some &quot;reasons&quot; they have to find the daughter of a Lord who was kidnapped by 3 men (men that are ghouls of a vampire) and in 8 hours, the kidnappers will set sail with this rescue expedition.<br /> So, the chapter 2 (in the chapter 1 PCs have to understand where the girl has been taken) is where they travel with the expedition's ships, looking for the girls. PCs don't know that the Franklin expedition left London not to looking for the &quot;Northwest Passage&quot;, but for something else... a creepier reason.<br /> <br /> 5 years later, the new expedition was sent not to find the ships, or at least, not only for this particular reason, but to bring the girl over there. Now, on these ships there will be coworkers of this vampire, both ghouls and a couple of brothers of him. On top of these, there are humans who were mentally deviated to help them. There are 8 ships and the girl would be placed in one of them but PCs won't know wich one. The trip would last 1-2 months.<br /> <br /> When the PCs can get on board of the ships? 2 choices:<br /> 1)The PCs would get on board before the expedition sails.<br /> 2)The PCs can't get on board in time and would reach the expedition weeks later.<br /> <br /> Why 2 choices you may ask? Well, their task is to find the girl (they will be helped by coworkers of the Lord, maybe the Lord himself). Playing a 2 months of travel and filling it up with horror and suprise would be difficult. Making them reaching the expedition later would mean i can narrate only few weeks of trip, making more dense of &quot;things&quot;. Would be more effective, in my opinion. Still, if the player would understand in time that the girl has been put on a ship and they would get on board in time, i have to be prepared. Or maybe i have to force them to not get on board in time, but i'm not a huge fan of &quot;technical constraints&quot;.<br /> <br /> In both cases, now there is my question: how to narrate this part of the travel?<br /> Just imagine the enviroment: you are in atlantic ocean, knowing that in one of the 8 ships there is the girl. People around you are strange. Day after day, you won't know anymore if you can trust the captain, the crew...Sometimes, one of your coworker disappears. You are surrounded by sense of danger and sometime you notice weird things happening: one mariner died in a strange way; the wind howls way too often; you see strange shadows lurking behind the corner; The captain of the ship clearly make you understand you are not welcome on board; during night, lanterns of the ships blink like some sort of message has been sent; some people seem to not soffer cold of atlantic ocean; and so on.<br /> Because i'm using historical informations, every ship has 70 men on it. Just a minor part of the crew is &quot;bound to serve the master&quot;, the vast majority of them think they are going to rescue the franklin expedition's crew.<br /> <br /> How do you create the sense of terror around the corner?<br /> How do you handle the investigation part?<br /> Consider that players don't know wich ship is the right one, but you can't reach another ship easily: they would have to steal a lifeboat, they could get caught, risking to be classified as mutineers; the ocean could be damn dangerous!<br /> Wich are some &quot;sovrannatural&quot; episodes that could be interesting?<br /> How to handle the flow of time without falling in the &quot;Another day has passed without nothing strange happened?&quot;<br /> How to stress players, make them feel alone and afraid?<br /> <br /> I'm afraid that is better on paper that on the table. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 05-11-2021, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T09:10:38-07:00","id":1448229,"title":"","content":"I have to admit to some confusion. As I understand it, the PCs are to recover the kidnapped daughter. This is a fine set up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a minor part of the crew is &quot;bound to serve the master&quot;, the vast majority of them think they are going to rescue the franklin expedition's crew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the girl on the same ship as the PCs? If so, then PCs sorting out the kidnappers and getting the girl back would be simple and quick. You post reads like the PCs, the kidnappers and the girl are all in the same group of ships. If that is the case then the PCs can probably recover the girl before they even leave the English channel.<br /> <br /> If the girl is the daughter of an English Lord, then that means money and social clout - so why not use that on the captains of the ships? Why not use that money and clout to make the captains and the officers cooperative in the search for the girl? This should be true even if the captain is a horses ass but not a slave to the vampire.<br /> <br /> I suggest the PCs do go to one or more of the captains, and a search is launched. But then the ship with the girl breaks from the others, and the remaining ships chase it towards the Franklin Expidition since every one is going the same direction anyway. But some of the agents and slaves of the vampires are still on the remaining ships, and in the chase the ships and the PCs have to deal with unseen enemies, bad weather, and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, some of those involved in the kidnapping may have magic at their disposal, and can call up fog, storms, and other problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-11-2021, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T09:18:23-07:00","id":1448230,"title":"","content":"so, 8 ships, leaving togheter. The girl is in one of them, but PCs don't know wich one. I need a strong reason why money and status wouldn't help delay the expedition (actually, there was a ceremony when franklin expedition left London, so could be the case that such an important expediction can't be delayed). In a certain way, some of the captains are compromised, so they won't say nothing about the girl. They could even try to take time untill the morning when they have to leave. That's is the primary scenario.<br /> Hope is clearer now<br /> <br /> about the break of one of the ship, could be a good idea too. Thanks, it's a good starting point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T09:38:08-07:00","id":1448234,"title":"","content":"A member of the royal family might pull rank on the nobleman, the girl's father, and order the expedition to set sail without searching for the daughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}